  "question": {
    "text": "A tower leans towards west making an angle <math><mi>&#945;</mi></math> with the vertical. The angular elevation of <math><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the top most point of the tower, is <math><msup><mrow><mn>75</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> as observed from a point <math><mi>C</mi></math> due east of <math><mi>A</mi></math> at a distance of&nbsp;<math><mn>20</mn></math> units. If the angular elevation of <math><mi>B&#160;</mi></math>from a point due east of <math><mi>C</mi></math> at a distance of&nbsp;<math><mn>20</mn></math>&nbsp;units&nbsp;from <math><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> then <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></mrow></math> is equal to"
  },
